  // shell (back disc, title block, panel, primary button, the right-hand drawer) and the Cards
  // category. The Backgrounds and Tables categories are measured on their own mockups by
  // ShopBackgroundsLayout (20) and ShopTablesLayout (21); ShopCustomizer assembles all three.
  //
  // Art: the shared kit and the ShopUI batch (ArtSource/Working/ShopUI/notes.md, rects from its
  // section 1 and 2): the panel is the plain kit card (slice unit 2.065 = sliceScale 0.898), the
  // tiles the light card (unit 2.66 = 1.157), the selected outline the thin kit line (unit 2.92 =
  // 1.27); the drawer, its discs and icons and the coin are the batch's pieces. The tiles,
  // pictures and labels below are measurement sources: ShopCustomizer turns each category's tile 0
  // into that category's three tiles, spaced as the three measured tiles are.
  //
  // The owner (5 Oct 2026): every category shows exactly three items and nothing scrolls, so the
  // mockups' chevrons, scroll track and "Swipe to browse" are not measured; the drawer is always
  // open, so its storefront disc and the divider under it are not either. ShopCustomizer narrows
  // the drawer and draws its three buttons smaller, stacked in its middle.
